%% alt: The attack surface in more detail. User prompts enter the application (1). Untrusted content from the web, email, uploads and other agents (2) and retrieval from documents and the vector store (3) enter context assembly, which goes through the AI gateway to the model provider. Model output goes through output handling; tool calls (4) pass a policy and identity check before reaching tools, MCP servers and business systems. The supply chain of models, packages and tool servers (5) feeds the model and the tools, and logs and traces (6) go to telemetry.
flowchart TB
  U[User]:::human -->|1 prompts| APP[Application]:::tool
  EXT[Web, email, uploads,<br/>other agents]:::untrusted -->|2 untrusted content| CTX
  KB[(Documents and<br/>vector store)]:::data -->|3 retrieval| CTX
  APP --> CTX[Context assembly]:::tool --> GW[AI gateway]:::control --> M[Model provider]:::model
  M --> OUT[Output handling]:::control
  OUT --> APP
  OUT -->|4 tool calls| POL{Policy and<br/>identity check}:::control --> T[Tools and MCP servers]:::tool --> SYS[(Business systems)]:::data
  SC[Models, packages,<br/>tool servers]:::untrusted -.->|5 supply chain| M
  SC -.-> T
  APP -->|6 logs, traces| LOG[(Telemetry)]:::data
